 "description": "Free preview of an exact-key one-to-one comparison of two explicitly mapped CSV/JSON tables. Complete dossier: 0.002 USDC on Base, JSON and CSV together. Maximum 500 combined rows and 48000 argument bytes. Default mode=amounts compares quantities with identical declared units and net/gross amounts (amount_basis and full mappings required). Use mode=fields for catalogue, inventory or CRM version comparison: each side maps keys only, and fields explicitly pairs left/right column names. No amount_basis, financial mapping, tolerances or FX options in fields mode. Returns added/removed rows and changed field values; exact normalized strings, null distinct from empty text, decimal spellings remain distinct. At most 19 compared fields, empty snapshots supported. Unmapped fields/schema changes ignored; no synchronization or inferred changes. Optional target_currency uses dated indicative ECB references (original data free). Never guess keys, aggregate split invoices or infer payment status. Ambiguous/invalid/incomparable rows block purchase. Ordinary differences and unmatched valid rows are findings. Save the private encrypted ticket before any optional purchase; MCP never signs or pays. Confirmed purchases recoverable for 24h from preview; pending settlement needs operator review, never repay.",
